n state lean and a Republican-leaning pollster field temper the margin, keeping it just short of Safe.", "watch": "A late turnout surge among Collins' rural base, or movement in the concurrent governor's race, could narrow the margin in the final days.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Jon Ossoff (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Senator Jon Ossoff seeks a second term against Representative Mike Collins in a state that leans slightly Republican but has favored Democrats in recent statewide contests. Ossoff has built an enormous financial advantage, raising nearly $116 million and holding over $15 million on hand, while Collins has struggled to keep pace with about $1.1 million in the bank. Outside spending on both sides remains modest so far.\n\nEvery recent poll shows Ossoff ahead, with margins ranging from six to fifteen points, and averages cluster near eight to nine points. Expert raters uniformly place the race in the Likely or Safe Democratic column, and prediction markets price Ossoff's chances at roughly 97 percent. Collins continues campaigning across the state, but the evidence points to a clear Ossoff advantage heading into Election Day.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9499, "margin": 8.78}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9449, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9229, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9348, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9317, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9355, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9397, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9457, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9522, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9495, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9478, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9479, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9545, "margin": 8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.928, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p